# Parked/superseded code - already-tracked files here stay tracked (gitignore
# doesn't untrack what's committed); this only stops new stray files from
# being swept into this folder by a future broad `git add`.
legacy_code/

# Packaging snapshots. Every zip in this repo is a handoff bundle of files that
# are already tracked individually (dB_target_sweeps/archive/*.zip,
# dB45_collection/dB45_collection.zip). They stay on disk for sharing; the tree
# is the source of truth, so committing them would just duplicate it.
*.zip

# Exception to `*.log` above: the 45 dB collection's solver run captures are the
# provenance for the resolved/unresolved gaps documented in
# dB45_collection/INTEGRATION_HANDOFF.md, so that folder is versioned whole.
!dB45_collection/logs/*.log

# Timestamped .bak snapshots taken before risky edits. Same reasoning as the
# zips above: these duplicate states that git already holds (or, for files being
# committed for the first time, states git holds from that commit onward), so
# versioning them would store the history twice. They stay on disk as a local
# undo buffer.
backups/
